Let a cross build name the target's LLVM program directory (POCL_TARGET_LLVM_BINDIR).

In a cross build PoCL looks for the target's clang, opt, llc ... in the
directory LLVMConfig.cmake reports (LLVM_TOOLS_BINARY_DIR), requires them
to exist there, and then strips CMAKE_SYSROOT from what it found to get
the path on the target, which it compiles in (CLANGCC, the name the Clang
driver is given). That assumes the target's LLVM is installed inside
CMAKE_SYSROOT. Here CMAKE_SYSROOT is the QNX SDP and the target's LLVM is
in a staging tree outside it; the toolchain file also keeps the staging
tree's bin directory out of every program search, because the programs in
it are QNX binaries that cannot run on the build machine. The configure
step stopped with "clang executable not found in <stage>/usr/local/bin!",
and had it found them the staging path would have been compiled into
libpocl.

POCL_TARGET_LLVM_BINDIR=<dir> names the directory the LLVM programs have on
the target; the names are recorded without searching. Without it nothing
changes.

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific

--- a/cmake/LLVM.cmake
+++ b/cmake/LLVM.cmake
@@ -224,7 +224,20 @@
 endif()
 
 
-if(CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING)
+if(CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING AND POCL_TARGET_LLVM_BINDIR)
+  # The directory the LLVM programs are in on the target, given by the user:
+  # for a target LLVM that is not installed below CMAKE_SYSROOT (a staging
+  # tree), where the search below cannot find the programs or cannot turn
+  # what it finds into the path on the target. Only the names are recorded.
+  message(STATUS "Target LLVM binaries are in ${POCL_TARGET_LLVM_BINDIR} on the target")
+  set(TARGET_CLANG "${POCL_TARGET_LLVM_BINDIR}/clang")
+  set(TARGET_CLANGXX "${POCL_TARGET_LLVM_BINDIR}/clang++")
+  set(TARGET_LLVM_OPT "${POCL_TARGET_LLVM_BINDIR}/opt")
+  set(TARGET_LLVM_LLC "${POCL_TARGET_LLVM_BINDIR}/llc")
+  set(TARGET_LLVM_AS "${POCL_TARGET_LLVM_BINDIR}/llvm-as")
+  set(TARGET_LLVM_DIS "${POCL_TARGET_LLVM_BINDIR}/llvm-dis")
+  set(TARGET_LLVM_LINK "${POCL_TARGET_LLVM_BINDIR}/llvm-link")
+elseif(CMAKE_CROSSCOMPILING)
   message(STATUS "Searching for Target LLVM binaries in ${LLVM_BINDIR}")
   # TODO how to handle LLVM_BINARY_SUFFIX ?
   set(SAVED_LLVM_BINARY_SUFFIX ${LLVM_BINARY_SUFFIX})
